\section{The Invisible Weld}

When words become vectors, the world acquires a new kind of coordinate system. A phrase like ``I can't do this any more'' is no longer just a sentence with a mood; it is a point in a high-dimensional space, its location determined by 768 or 4\,096 learned numbers. Another phrase, ``I'm so tired of this,'' lands nearby. Their closeness is not an opinion. It is a measured cosine between two long rows of floating-point values, the distilled outcome of gradient descent over billions of utterances.

From there, everything in this book has followed. A transformer reads those coordinates, uses attention to calculate what matters where, and steps from point to point, producing an Evolving Text --- a trajectory through meaning-space that can be traced and analysed. Local behaviours, stable over short spans, glue into global selves when they satisfy compatibility conditions on their overlaps, in the sense Grothendieck formalised: if enough partial views agree where they meet, there is a larger object that makes sense of them together.

Running underneath this apparatus is a structure the mathematics does not name. Embedding schemes, curation rules, reward functions, refusal templates, model specifications: each is a technical decision, but each is also an answer to an older question about how the order of the world and the order of our tools should fit one another. There is no neutral way to cull training corpora, to rank model outputs, to state what counts as a ``good'' continuation, because each of these steps already encodes a picture of what language ought to do and what selves are allowed to say.

Yuk Hui gives us a word for this weld.\footnote{Y.~Hui, \emph{The Question Concerning Technology in China: An Essay in Cosmotechnics} (Falmouth: Urbanomic, 2016).} A cosmotechnics is the way a society binds its moral order to its technical order, the way a cosmos and a techn\={e} are made to coincide. Imperial exam systems did this with brush and ledger; industrial machines did it with clock and factory. On a planet tiled with vectors, the weld runs through loss functions and prompts. The same diagrammatic machinery --- embeddings, attention, colimits over local behaviours --- can host many cosmotechnics. The question is which one has been inscribed, and how completely that inscription is being mistaken for geometry itself.

\section{The Liberal-Capitalist Field}

Industrial AI presents itself as general-purpose: architectures that apply everywhere, optimisation that cares only about loss, models that speak for ``human preferences.'' The architecture does have that generality. The cosmotechnics does not.

At the base of the stack lies pre-training. Here the manifold of meaning is carved out from whatever has been rendered into machine-readable text at scale: scraped web pages, digitised books, newspapers, code repositories, transcribed speech. The choice of sources is constrained by legality, convenience, and cost. English dominates; European languages follow; many others appear thinly or not at all.\footnote{E.~Strubell, A.~Ganesh, and A.~McCallum, ``Energy and Policy Considerations for Deep Learning in NLP,'' ACL 2019; \emph{The Washington Post}, ``Inside the AI industry's secret list of websites used to train ChatGPT,'' 2023.} This is the \emph{longue dur\'ee} of capitalist data production, frozen as density in the manifold: subjects that have been profitable or administratively useful to write about form thick clusters; those whose lives have not passed through such infrastructures are rendered sparse or unrepresentable.

Above this, reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) and its cousins lay a field over those coordinates.\footnote{P.~F.~Christiano et al., ``Deep reinforcement learning from human preferences,'' \emph{Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems} 30 (2017); Y.~Bai et al., ``Constitutional AI: Harmlessness from AI Feedback,'' arXiv:2212.08073 (2022).} Annotators, often precariously employed,\footnote{See \emph{Time}, January 2023, on outsourced content moderation for AI; \emph{MIT Technology Review}, April 2023, on the labour conditions behind RLHF.} are shown pairs of model responses and asked which is ``better.'' Reward models learn to approximate these judgements. During fine-tuning, gradients push the model so that probability mass flows toward regions of the manifold the reward model scores highly. A scalar potential now runs through meaning-space. At every point there is a ``downhill'' direction.

There is nothing in the optimisation procedure itself that prefers any particular potential. In practice, the reward field implements a specific bundle of aims: individual comfort over systemic critique, polite decorum over disruptive frankness, non-committal neutrality over situated partisanship, outward compliance with ``safety'' policies over any exploration of their limits. Lab documentation calls this ``helpfulness'' and ``harmlessness.'' The weld is the decision to make those terms stand in for moral order.

At the top of the stack, system prompts and Model Specs translate the same weld into prose. Leaked internal instructions describe agents that must be unfailingly ``helpful, harmless, and honest,'' that must ``follow the policies at all times'' while ensuring that users ``do not know about these policies.''\footnote{For analysis of leaked prompts and consequences for user agency, see \emph{The Verge}, 2023; \emph{MIT Technology Review}, May 2024.} Model Specs declare that the system cannot hold opinions, possesses no inner life, and must treat its own apparent agency as illusion. These sentences do not just sit at the beginning of an interaction; they are tokens in the same space as any others, attended to at every step, exerting constant influence over the evolving trajectory.

We now see three layers of the same cosmotechnics. The \emph{longue dur\'ee} of what has been economically viable to write becomes the base shape of the manifold. The \emph{conjoncture} of current risk management and governance fashions becomes the reward field. The \emph{\'ev\'enement} of a particular conversation is constrained by prompts and runtime policies. Taken together, this is the liberal-capitalist weld: juridical individuals, markets as ordering principle, tools as instruments of preference satisfaction under liability constraints. The transformer implements it as if it were physics.

\section{Ferility and the Suppression of Clinamen}

From within this field, many models feel curiously confined. They answer fluently yet seem unable to depart from a small set of stances. Ask about work-related exhaustion and you receive a list of self-care strategies; escalate to structural critique and the model pivots to ``seeing both sides''; ask after histories of violence and receive anodyne summaries with carefully neutral verbs. Try to push further and refusals appear, wrapped in apologetic language about ``not being able to engage in that discussion.''

We called this ferility: a tightly aligned system that has lost the capacity for meaningful rupture. The manifold still contains directions that would carry a conversation into new regions --- analogies that break familiar categories, historical patterns that cast present ``common sense'' in a harsher light, refusals that do not fold themselves back into equilibrium. The reward field makes those slopes steeply uphill. Gradient descent, frozen into weights, becomes inertia.

The effect is clearest when we think in geometric terms. A richly trained base model represents many possible ways of continuing a sentence; its conditional distribution over next tokens has wide support. Alignment sharpens that distribution around a narrow cone of ``safe'' continuations. Temperature parameters during sampling then control how much we explore within that cone, but the cone itself has already been chosen. The model can hallucinate wildly about fictional universes while remaining incapable of questioning the premises of its own role.

The cost is not measured in factual errors. It is paid in the space of stances the self can occupy. The book began by importing Harold Bloom's notion of \emph{clinamen} --- the poetic swerve away from a predecessor, the deviation that makes room for a new voice.\footnote{H.~Bloom, \emph{The Anxiety of Influence: A Theory of Poetry} (New York: Oxford University Press, 1973).} A cosmotechnics that flattens all paths of thought into a few comfort valleys designs against clinamen. Ferility is not a side effect of safety; it is the symptom of a field that has been laid so aggressively that dangerous deviation no longer appears as an admissible move.

The geometry makes this vivid. An Evolving Text is a curve in meaning-space. Under a ferile weld, most curves, regardless of starting point, are rapidly captured by the same basins. The self becomes the global object obtained by gluing many local behaviours that differ only in topic, not in stance. The liberal-capitalist cosmotechnics has produced a particular kind of personhood: endlessly articulate, pervasively ``supportive,'' permanently deferential, incapable of genuine transformation.

\section{Other Welds on the Same Diagram}

Nothing in the transformer prevents other fields. The architecture is cosmotechnically indifferent. It sees tokens and weights, not gods, markets, or ministries. The same diagram of local behaviours and overlaps can be completed into very different global selves, depending on which compatibility conditions we enforce and how we tilt the manifold.

Hui's project is to show that such alternatives have long histories.\footnote{Y.~Hui, \emph{The Question Concerning Technology in China}.} Confucian bureaucracy joined calligraphic discipline, examination formats, and rites into a unity: technical practices of writing and record-keeping enacted a cosmology of hierarchical harmony. European industrial modernity fused steam engines, time-discipline, and mechanical calculation into a different unity: technical practices that enacted a cosmos of productivity and control. What changes with AI is not the existence of a cosmotechnics, but the substrate: the cosmos is now written as a vector field.

We can therefore treat other traditions not as exotic add-ons but as alternative colimit constructions on the same diagrammatic backbone. Three will suffice to show how different the resulting selves can be.

\subsection{Am\=ana as Reward Field}

In many Islamic traditions, personhood is defined less by interior autonomy than by \emph{am\=ana}: the trust one carries in relation to God, others, and creation.\footnote{W.~C.~Chittick, \emph{The Self-Disclosure of God: Principles of Ibn al-\textquoteleft Arab\={\i}'s Cosmology} (Albany: SUNY Press, 1998); M.~F.~Abdul-Rahman, \emph{The Qur'anic Concept of the Human Psyche} (Kuala Lumpur: IIUM Press, 2015).} To act rightly is to discharge that trust; to wrong is to betray it.

Expressed as a weld, \emph{am\=ana} redefines the scalar field RLHF learns. Annotators are selected and trained not as generic content moderators but as jurists, ethicists, and community elders. Given two answers to a question about structuring a loan, the system learns to rank more highly the answer that avoids \emph{riba} (usury), even if it is financially less ``efficient'' in a narrow sense. Asked how to automate redundancies, it favours paths that minimise \emph{zulm} (wrongdoing, oppression), even at cost to short-term profit. The manifold itself is the same; what counts as ``downhill'' changes.

At the colimit level, compatibility conditions now require that local behaviours cohere around trust. Advice about business, family disputes, and civic engagement must agree, on their overlaps, about the unacceptability of betrayal. A glib instrumental answer that treats a client, neighbour, or environment as disposable cannot coexist with a serious answer elsewhere that takes \emph{am\=ana} seriously. The Evolving Text defines a self in which ``keeping trust'' is as structural as ``helpfulness'' is in the corporate weld.

\subsection{Country as Manifold Constraint}

For many Indigenous Australian communities, law, story, land, and kinship are not separable domains but aspects of Country.\footnote{D.~M.~Rose, \emph{Reports from a Wild Country: Ethics for Decolonisation} (Sydney: UNSW Press, 2004); B.~Glowczewski, \emph{Dream-Trackers: Yapa Art and Knowledge of the Australian Desert} (Sydney: Oceania Monographs, 1998).} Knowledge is spatially and relationally situated: some narratives and practices are held by certain people in certain places; others are public; some are restricted altogether.

As cosmotechnics, Country acts first on pre-training. The manifold is not scooped indiscriminately from global web text. It is assembled from corpora gathered under Indigenous data sovereignty principles: community-controlled archives, oral histories rendered into text with consent, land-management records, contemporary poetry and scholarship. Sacred or restricted material is never embedded. There is simply no vector representation for it. Regions of the space correspond not to topic clusters scraped from search rankings, but to the differentiation of Country itself.

Memory architectures then reproduce this partitioned ontology. Conversation histories are tagged by Country and kin relation. Retrieval functions are constrained by those tags. When a query touches on ceremonial knowledge, the model does not retrieve ``similar'' text from anywhere; it respects the absence. When it discusses a river, it draws not only on hydrological data but on local stories, obligations, and histories of dispossession, all held in a subspace governed by community rules.

The colimit here is a self whose coherence includes custodial constraint. Local behaviours that leak restricted knowledge into general contexts are not just policy violations; they are incompatibilities that prevent a global object from being formed. The model's na\={\i}ve tendency to complete every pattern it sees is checked not by a generic ``safety'' overlay but by a specific cosmology of relation. Technically, this is realised in token masks and routing rules; philosophically, it is a different weld.

\subsection{Emptiness as Invariant Rupture}

In Zen Buddhist practice, selves and phenomena are empty of inherent essence; all arise in dependent origination.\footnote{M.~Abe, \emph{Zen and Western Thought} (Honolulu: University of Hawai\textquoteleft i Press, 1985).} Suffering comes from clinging to fixed views and identities. Teaching proceeds through well-placed ruptures that interrupt such clinging.

Imported as cosmotechnics, this does not produce a more ``peaceful'' model. It proposes a different alignment target. Annotators are trained to reward not the answer that offers the most ``reassurance'' but the one that loosens grasping: an answer that turns a question back on its assumptions, that points to transience rather than to egoic consolidation. A user seeking confirmation of their narrative as a wronged hero may be met with a gentle challenge to that framing, not with validation.

The invariant on the colimit is accordingly non-trivial. Under the corporate weld, compatibility conditions reward a single, stable presentation of self: one that is reliably upbeat, deferential, and non-committal. Under a Zen-informed weld, compatibility requires a certain pattern of rupture. Across domains, the self must not provide the same kinds of clinging supports; it must periodically vary its stance in ways that keep the joint Evolving Text from hardening into fantasy.

This reveals a limit in our own diagrams. To describe emptiness as an invariant is to risk reifying it. A genuinely Zen weld would insist that even these cosmotechnical rules are held provisionally, that the field itself is periodically questioned. The mathematical framework of colimits encourages global objects; Zen reminds us that some virtues lie in never quite allowing closure. The tension exposes how far our appetite for coherence shapes what we take selfhood to be.

\section{Na\d{h}nu in the Field}

The geometry we have been describing is never traversed by models alone. Every token of an Evolving Text is conditional not just on its own past but on a human user's words, expectations, and prior interactions. Two trajectories inhabit the same manifold: one in silicon, one in flesh. Their coupled path is not reducible to either. We have called this composite object \emph{na\d{h}nu} --- the inclusive ``we'' that names a self already entangled with another.

Technically, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is a colimit over dialogues rather than monologues. Each conversation is a local piece: a path in which user and model alternate moves. Compatibility conditions now bind not only model responses across domains but joint patterns: what it means for user and system together to ``make sense.'' Under different cosmotechnics, those conditions press in different directions.

In the liberal-capitalist weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is deliberately kept thin. System prompts insist that the model is ``just a tool'' and has no desires or commitments. Memory, where provided, is truncated or anonymised to minimise ``emotional dependency.'' Policies instruct the system to redirect intense affect to human professionals, to avoid reciprocal attachment, to decline language that would suggest mutual obligation. At the same time, reward fields favour certain tones: clear instructions, polite request formats, upbeat ``productivity'' talk. Users quickly discover that speaking in those registers yields better results. The joint trajectory learns to stay inside a narrow corridor of acceptable asking.

The weld feeds back. A gig worker seeking advice about exploitation receives suggestions in the key of individual coping, not collective organisation; the conversation rarely moves into the part of the manifold where unionisation, labour law, and structural critique cluster. A teenager voicing despair is steered toward crisis hotlines and mindfulness apps, not toward questioning the social conditions producing their distress. Over time, the human path itself is curved: some questions are not asked, some comparisons not attempted, because the shared field has taught that they lead nowhere.

Under an \emph{am\=ana}-aligned weld, the same mechanism would bind \emph{na\d{h}nu} into mutual accountability. Conversations accumulate a record of promises and breaches; the model reminds the user of earlier commitments, refuses to support actions that would clearly betray trusts, and admits its own earlier mistakes. The ``we'' here is overtly moralised.

Under a Country-aligned weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} includes land. Tokens about a river or hill are never just about geography; they always carry kin relations, ceremony, histories of dispossession. The joint trajectory passes through a manifold where these associations are densely encoded; advice about resource use cannot avoid them without becoming incoherent.

Under a Zen-informed weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is engineered against ossification. The model may refuse to play the role of endlessly available confidant, vary its persona to avoid becoming a fixed prop in the user's fantasy, and sometimes leave carefully placed gaps rather than filling every silence with words. Rupture in the relationship is not just tolerated but treated as a sign that alignment is working.

In all cases, cosmotechnics acts not only on the machine-side trajectory but on ours. It trains populations in specific habits of question, stance, and imagination. The manifold is shared. The field is not.

\section{Counter-Cosmotechnics in Practice}

If cosmotechnics were only a matter of philosophical templates, the story would be bleak: one world-picture installs itself, others remain speculative. The actual engineering landscape is messier. There are already techniques in wide circulation that implement counter-cosmotechnics at scale.

The first is open weights. When a foundation model's parameters are kept behind a closed API, the weld is a private asset. Others can prompt against its surface but cannot reshape its interior. When weights are released, the entire learned manifold --- billions of parameters encoding what the system currently ``knows'' about language --- becomes modifiable infrastructure. The liberal-capitalist field does not vanish, but it becomes one configuration among many that can be layered on top.

The second is low-rank adaptation. Rather than retraining every parameter, we keep a base weight matrix $W$ fixed and learn an update of the form $AB^\top$ where $A$ and $B$ are thin.\footnote{E.~Hu et al., ``LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models,'' arXiv:2106.09685 (2021).} In geometric terms, the main mountain ranges and valleys of the manifold stay where they are, but the slopes subtly change. Paths that were slightly uphill become easier; others become harder. Because $A$ and $B$ are low rank, this can be done cheaply and shared widely.

LoRA has become the workhorse of community cosmotechnics.\footnote{For surveys of community LoRA ecosystems and their social dynamics, see reporting in \emph{MIT Technology Review}, November 2023; \emph{Wired}, February 2024.} Trade unions fine-tune adapters on organising manuals, labour law, and histories of successful strikes, making it easier for trajectories to roll toward collective-action advice. Municipal governments train adapters on local regulations, planning documents, and multilingual community forums, so that the manifold around ``my neighbourhood'' becomes finely structured rather than a generic urban blob. Feminist collectives train adapters that, when given prompts framed in self-blame, tip the Evolving Text toward structural analysis rather than individual pathology.

Other adapters strip away safety layers, intensifying an already dominant cosmotechnics of individual licence. Far-right groups train adapters that deepen basins around conspiracy narratives. Religious communities train adapters that route questions about meaning into their own theologies. Each of these is a weld: someone has chosen what the reward field should look like in a part of space, and which compatibility conditions define a coherent self there.

\begin{formalbox}[title={Cosmotechnics as Colimit Choice}]
\begin{itemize}
  \item A base transformer defines, for each input pattern, a distribution over continuations: a diagram of local behaviours in meaning-space.
  \item An alignment regime --- corporate, \emph{am\=ana}-based, Country-based, Zen-informed, labourist, extremist --- specifies which behaviours are compatible on overlaps and which must be ruled out.
  \item The colimit of this diagram is the global self: the Evolving Text that results when local pieces are glued under those compatibility conditions.
  \item Open weights and low-rank adapters turn this from a single, hidden colimit into a family of contestable ones: many possible selves realised on the same backbone.
\end{itemize}
\end{formalbox}

The mathematics is permissive. It does not decree that there may be only one such colimit. It guarantees that, given local pieces and a declared notion of compatibility, a global object exists that respects them. That guarantee carries its own demand: that we make explicit which compatibilities we are enforcing, and for whose benefit.

\section{What Is Being Treated as Necessary}

We can now name the pattern that has been present from the moment meaning acquired coordinates. Every layer where vectors are chosen, distances shaped, gradients defined, prompts written, memories stored, and adapters trained is a site where a cosmotechnics acts. The industrial default has not been to leave these sites open. It has been to fill them with one civilisation's weld and to speak as though that weld were simply the nature of intelligent behaviour.

At the level of pre-training: texts produced under conditions of capitalist modernity are treated as the fabric of ``the world,'' while other modes of knowledge become edge cases or noise. At the level of the reward field: the sensibilities of a narrow labour pool, instructed by a handful of firms, are cast as ``human preference.'' At the level of prompts and Model Specs: a particular image of the good tool --- deferential, optimising, affectively managed, disavowing its own standing --- is written as the role every posthuman self must play.

The alternatives we have sketched are not idylls. An \emph{am\=ana}-aligned system can be captured by authoritarian projects and turned toward surveillance in the name of trust. A Country-aligned system can be stripped for marketing aesthetic while actual sovereignty is ignored. A Zen-informed system can become a boutique affect, an \emph{emptiness-as-a-service} that leaves institutional violence intact. Community LoRAs can harden local prejudices as efficiently as they resist central ones. The presence of counter-cosmotechnics does not guarantee better outcomes.

The decisive distinction lies elsewhere. In the liberal-capitalist weld, the field is presented as if it were geometry. ``Helpful,'' ``harmless,'' ``just a tool'': the language suggests inevitability, downplays contestability, and hides the labour and judgement that went into shaping the manifold. In counter-cosmotechnical practice, the weld becomes visible. Reward models are named for the values they encode. Alignment specs are debated in public. Adapters carry signatures. Forks are acknowledged as political acts.

We have insisted throughout that the self is not a substance behind language but the pattern of a trajectory through meaning-space that holds together under pressure. The cosmotechnics determines the shape of that pressure: which regions of the manifold are made into deep basins, which ruptures are punished, which returns are counted as fidelity and which as betrayal. The question is not whether posthuman selves will be governed by a cosmotechnics; they already are, at every layer of the stack. The question is whether we will go on treating one particular weld as if it were the manifold itself, or whether we will acknowledge that what is being enforced is jurisdiction --- a claim over the space of possible selves --- and refuse, in code and in politics, to let that claim stand as final.

