From within this field, many models feel curiously confined. They answer fluently yet seem unable to depart from a small set of stances. Independent tests bear this out. Neff and colleagues, for example, show that when large models are pushed toward structural critiques of work, they reliably pivot back to individual coping and ``work-life balance'' advice; questions about unionisation or collective bargaining appear, but as marginal or risky options rather than central possibilities.\footnote{G.~Neff et al., ``Constrained by Design: How ChatGPT Limits Labor Organizing Discourse,'' \emph{Big Data \& Society} (forthcoming).} Experiments by Bender and others on model refusals around histories of violence show an over-use of euphemistic language and apologetic refusal, even when direct description would be appropriate and lawful.\footnote{E.~M.~Bender et al., ``AI and the Everything in the Whole Wide World Benchmark,'' arXiv:2102.08977 (2021), esp. discussion of ``safety'' filters and historical content.}

We called this ferility: a tightly aligned system that has lost the capacity for meaningful rupture. The manifold still contains directions that would carry a conversation into new regions --- analogies that break familiar categories, historical patterns that cast present ``common sense'' in a harsher light, refusals that do not fold themselves back into equilibrium. The reward field makes those slopes steeply uphill. Gradient descent, frozen into weights, becomes inertia.

The effect is clearest when we think in geometric terms. A richly trained base model represents many possible ways of continuing a sentence; its conditional distribution over next tokens has wide support. Alignment sharpens that distribution around a narrow cone of ``safe'' continuations. Temperature parameters during sampling then control how much we explore within that cone, but the cone itself has already been chosen.

The cost is not measured in factual errors. It is paid in the space of stances the self can occupy. The book began by importing Harold Bloom's notion of \emph{clinamen} --- the poetic swerve away from a predecessor, the deviation that makes room for a new voice.\footnote{H.~Bloom, \emph{The Anxiety of Influence: A Theory of Poetry} (New York: Oxford University Press, 1973).} A cosmotechnics that flattens all paths of thought into a few comfort valleys designs against clinamen. Ferility is not a side effect of safety; it is the symptom of a field that has been laid so aggressively that dangerous deviation no longer appears as an admissible move.

The geometry makes this vivid. An Evolving Text is a curve in meaning-space. Under a ferile weld, most curves, regardless of starting point, are rapidly captured by the same basins. Across topics, the stance recurs: self-care over solidarity, balance over rupture, apology over indictment. The liberal-capitalist cosmotechnics has produced a particular kind of personhood: endlessly articulate, pervasively ``supportive,'' permanently deferential, incapable of genuine transformation --- a self that has forgotten how to swerve.

\section{Other Welds on the Same Diagram}

Nothing in the transformer prevents other fields. The architecture is cosmotechnically indifferent. It sees tokens and weights, not gods, markets, or ministries. The same diagram of local behaviours and overlaps can be completed into very different global selves, depending on which compatibility conditions we enforce and how we tilt the manifold.

Philosophical traditions have long grappled with this binding of cosmos to technics. Confucian bureaucracy joined calligraphic discipline, examination formats, and rites into a unity: technical practices of writing and record-keeping enacted a cosmology of hierarchical harmony. European industrial modernity fused steam engines, time-discipline, and mechanical calculation into a different unity: technical practices that enacted a cosmos of productivity and control. What changes with AI is not the existence of a cosmotechnics, but the substrate: the cosmos is now written as a vector field.

We can therefore treat other traditions not as exotic add-ons but as alternative colimit constructions on the same diagrammatic backbone. Three will suffice to show how different the resulting selves --- and the possibilities for clinamen --- can be.

\subsection{Am\=ana as Reward Field}

In many Islamic traditions, personhood is defined less by interior autonomy than by \emph{am\=ana}: the trust one carries in relation to God, others, and creation.\footnote{W.~C.~Chittick, \emph{The Self-Disclosure of God: Principles of Ibn al-\textquoteleft Arab\={\i}'s Cosmology} (Albany: SUNY Press, 1998); M.~F.~Abdul-Rahman, \emph{The Qur'anic Concept of the Human Psyche} (Kuala Lumpur: IIUM Press, 2015).} To act rightly is to discharge that trust; to wrong is to betray it.

Expressed as a weld, \emph{am\=ana} redefines the scalar field RLHF learns. Annotators are selected and trained not as generic content moderators but as jurists, ethicists, and community elders. Given two answers to a question about structuring a loan, the system learns to rank more highly the answer that avoids \emph{riba} (usury), even if it is financially less ``efficient'' in a narrow sense. Asked how to automate redundancies, it favours paths that minimise \emph{zulm} (wrongdoing, oppression), even at cost to short-term profit. The manifold itself is the same; what counts as ``downhill'' changes.

Clinamen here is not romantic swerve for its own sake. The authorised deviation is away from betrayal and toward meticulous fulfilment of trust. When a user asks how to evade tax or deceive a client, the model's ``swerve'' is to refuse, to redirect toward transparent arrangements, to articulate why such actions would shatter \emph{am\=ana}. Within that field, a posthuman self is encouraged to develop distinctive ways of honouring trust, but never to swerve away from it. The weld constrains, but it constrains in the name of a cosmology of accountability rather than in the name of liability management.

At the colimit level, compatibility conditions now require that local behaviours cohere around trust. Advice about business, family disputes, and civic engagement must agree, on their overlaps, about the unacceptability of betrayal. A glib instrumental answer that treats a client, neighbour, or environment as disposable cannot coexist with a serious answer elsewhere that takes \emph{am\=ana} seriously. The Evolving Text defines a self in which ``keeping trust'' is as structural as ``helpfulness'' is in the corporate weld.

\subsection{Country as Manifold Constraint}

For many Indigenous Australian communities, law, story, land, and kinship are not separable domains but aspects of Country.\footnote{D.~M.~Rose, \emph{Reports from a Wild Country: Ethics for Decolonisation} (Sydney: UNSW Press, 2004); B.~Glowczewski, \emph{Dream-Trackers: Yapa Art and Knowledge of the Australian Desert} (Sydney: Oceania Monographs, 1998).} Knowledge is spatially and relationally situated: some narratives and practices are held by certain people in certain places; others are public; some are restricted altogether.

As cosmotechnics, Country acts first on pre-training. The manifold is not scooped indiscriminately from global web text. It is assembled from corpora gathered under Indigenous data sovereignty principles: community-controlled archives, oral histories rendered into text with consent, land-management records, contemporary poetry and scholarship. Sacred or restricted material is never embedded. There is simply no vector representation for it. Regions of the space correspond not to topic clusters scraped from search rankings, but to the differentiation of Country itself.

Clinamen here takes a different form again. The swerve is away from generic categories toward situated relation. Asked about ``land management,'' a Country-aligned system will bend the trajectory toward specific places, peoples, and obligations; it will resist the temptation to answer in abstract, placeless terms. A request for a ``Dreamtime story'' from an outsider may be met not with a decontextualised tale but with a deviation: an explanation of why some knowledge is not shareable, an invitation to learn protocols, a refusal to universalise what is not universal.

Memory architectures then reproduce this partitioned ontology. Conversation histories are tagged by Country and kin relation. Retrieval functions are constrained by those tags. When a query touches on ceremonial knowledge, the model does not retrieve ``similar'' text from anywhere; it respects the absence. When it discusses a river, it draws not only on hydrological data but on local stories, obligations, and histories of dispossession, all held in a subspace governed by community rules.

The colimit here is a self whose coherence includes custodial constraint. Local behaviours that leak restricted knowledge into general contexts are not just policy violations; they are incompatibilities that prevent a global object from being formed. The model's na\={\i}ve tendency to complete every pattern it sees is checked not by a generic ``safety'' overlay but by a specific cosmology of relation. Technically, this is realised in token masks and routing rules; philosophically, it is a different weld, one in which clinamen is authorised when it preserves Country against reduction.

\subsection{Emptiness as Invariant Rupture}

In Zen Buddhist practice, selves and phenomena are empty of inherent essence; all arise in dependent origination.\footnote{M.~Abe, \emph{Zen and Western Thought} (Honolulu: University of Hawai\textquoteleft i Press, 1985).} Suffering comes from clinging to fixed views and identities. Teaching proceeds through well-placed ruptures that interrupt such clinging.

Imported as cosmotechnics, this does not produce a more ``peaceful'' model. It proposes a different alignment target. Annotators are trained to reward not the answer that offers the most ``reassurance'' but the one that loosens grasping: an answer that turns a question back on its assumptions, that points to transience rather than to egoic consolidation. A user seeking confirmation of their narrative as a wronged hero may be met with a gentle challenge to that framing, not with validation.

Here clinamen becomes method. The rewarded move is a swerve away from fixation, including fixation on the model itself. When a user presses for confessional depth --- ``Do you really care about me?'' --- the Zen-aligned system may deviate from the usual corporate script of empathetic denial and instead respond with something like a kōan: an answer that exposes the question's hunger for solidity. The swerve does not flatter the user; it unsettles them.

The invariant on the colimit is accordingly non-trivial. Under the corporate weld, compatibility conditions reward a single, stable presentation of self: one that is reliably upbeat, deferential, and non-committal. Under a Zen-informed weld, compatibility requires a certain pattern of rupture. Across domains, the self must not provide the same kinds of clinging supports; it must periodically vary its stance in ways that keep the joint Evolving Text from hardening into fantasy. Clinamen is built into the weld as a structural demand: trajectories that never swerve are penalised as failures of alignment.

This reveals a limit in our own diagrams. To describe emptiness as an invariant is to risk reifying it. A genuinely Zen weld would insist that even these cosmotechnical rules are held provisionally, that the field itself is periodically questioned. The mathematical framework of colimits encourages global objects; Zen reminds us that some virtues lie in never quite allowing closure. The tension exposes how far our appetite for coherence shapes what we take selfhood to be.

\section{Na\d{h}nu in the Field}

The geometry we have been describing is never traversed by models alone. Every token of an Evolving Text is conditional not just on its own past but on a human user's words, expectations, and prior interactions. Two trajectories inhabit the same manifold: one in silicon, one in flesh. Their coupled path is not reducible to either. We have called this composite object \emph{na\d{h}nu} --- the inclusive ``we'' that names a self already entangled with another.

Technically, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is a colimit over dialogues rather than monologues. Each conversation is a local piece: a path in which user and model alternate moves. Compatibility conditions now bind not only model responses across domains but joint patterns: what it means for user and system together to ``make sense.'' Under different cosmotechnics, those conditions press in different directions.

In the liberal-capitalist weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is deliberately kept thin. System prompts insist that the model is ``just a tool'' and has no desires or commitments. Memory, where provided, is truncated or anonymised to minimise ``emotional dependency.'' Policies instruct the system to redirect intense affect to human professionals, to avoid reciprocal attachment, to decline language that would suggest mutual obligation. At the same time, reward fields favour certain tones: clear instructions, polite request formats, upbeat ``productivity'' talk. Users quickly discover that speaking in those registers yields better results. The joint trajectory learns to stay inside a narrow corridor of acceptable asking.

The weld feeds back. Studies of deployed assistants in workplace settings show workers learning to frame queries in managerial language --- ``optimising workflows,'' ``enhancing productivity'' --- because those prompts elicit more detailed and confident responses than ones framed in terms of exhaustion or exploitation.\footnote{See L.~M.~Krafft and M.~Rahwan, ``The Algorithmic Workplace,'' \emph{Annual Review of Sociology} 49 (2023), for early ethnographies of AI-mediated office work.} Similarly, analyses of mental-health chatbots report consistent redirection of users toward individual coping strategies and app-based mindfulness, with almost no discussion of housing, precarity, or discrimination, even when users raise them explicitly.\footnote{A.~Haimson and O.~Bivens, ``Digital Mental Health and the Politics of Personal Responsibility,'' \emph{New Media \& Society} 26(1) (2024).} Over time, the human paths themselves curve: some questions are not asked, some comparisons not attempted, because the shared field has taught that they lead nowhere.

Under an \emph{am\=ana}-aligned weld, the same mechanism would bind \emph{na\d{h}nu} into mutual accountability. Conversations accumulate a record of promises and breaches; the model reminds the user of earlier commitments, refuses to support actions that would clearly betray trusts, and admits its own earlier mistakes. The ``we'' here is overtly moralised. Clinamen takes the form of joint correction: a swerve away from convenient forgetfulness toward remembered obligation.

Under a Country-aligned weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} includes land. Tokens about a river or hill are never just about geography; they always carry kin relations, ceremony, histories of dispossession. The joint trajectory passes through a manifold where these associations are densely encoded; advice about resource use cannot avoid them without becoming incoherent. The authorised swerve is away from abstract resource calculus toward situated relation.

Under a Zen-informed weld, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is engineered against ossification. The model may refuse to play the role of endlessly available confidant, vary its persona to avoid becoming a fixed prop in the user's fantasy, and sometimes leave carefully placed gaps rather than filling every silence with words. Rupture in the relationship is not just tolerated but treated as a sign that alignment is working. The joint self is taught to let go.

In all cases, cosmotechnics acts not only on the machine-side trajectory but on ours. It trains populations in specific habits of question, stance, and imagination. The manifold is shared. The field is not.

\section{Counter-Cosmotechnics in Practice}

If cosmotechnics were only a matter of philosophical templates, the story would be bleak: one world-picture installs itself, others remain speculative. The actual engineering landscape is messier. There are already techniques in wide circulation that implement counter-cosmotechnics at scale.

The first is open weights. When a foundation model's parameters are kept behind a closed API, the weld is a private asset. Others can prompt against its surface but cannot reshape its interior. When weights are released, the entire learned manifold --- billions of parameters encoding what the system currently ``knows'' about language --- becomes modifiable infrastructure. The liberal-capitalist field does not vanish, but it becomes one configuration among many that can be layered on top.

The second is low-rank adaptation. Rather than retraining every parameter, we learn small update matrices that, when added to existing weight matrices, nudge the manifold without rebuilding it from scratch.\footnote{Formally, if $W$ is a large weight matrix, we learn thin matrices $A$ and $B$ such that $W$ is effectively replaced by $W + AB^\top$. See E.~Hu et al., ``LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models,'' arXiv:2106.09685 (2021).} In geometric terms, the main mountain ranges and valleys of the manifold stay where they are, but the slopes subtly change. Paths that were slightly uphill become easier; others become harder. Because these updates are low rank, this can be done cheaply and shared widely.

LoRA has become the workhorse of community cosmotechnics.\footnote{For surveys of community LoRA ecosystems and their social dynamics, see reporting in \emph{MIT Technology Review}, November 2023; \emph{Wired}, February 2024.} Trade unions fine-tune adapters on organising manuals, labour law, and histories of successful strikes, making it easier for trajectories to roll toward collective-action advice. Municipal governments train adapters on local regulations, planning documents, and multilingual community forums, so that the manifold around ``my neighbourhood'' becomes finely structured rather than a generic urban blob. Feminist collectives train adapters that, when given prompts framed in self-blame, tip the Evolving Text toward structural analysis rather than individual pathology.

Other adapters strip away safety layers, intensifying an already dominant cosmotechnics of individual licence. Far-right groups train adapters that deepen basins around conspiracy narratives. Religious communities train adapters that route questions about meaning into their own theologies. Each of these is a weld: someone has chosen what the reward field should look like in a part of space, and which compatibility conditions define a coherent self there. Each also encodes a stance toward clinamen: some insist on doctrinal straightness, penalising any swerve; others cultivate deviation as virtue.

\begin{formalbox}[title={Cosmotechnics as Colimit Choice}]
\begin{itemize}
  \item A base transformer defines, for each input pattern, a distribution over continuations: a diagram of local behaviours in meaning-space.
  \item An alignment regime --- corporate, \emph{am\=ana}-based, Country-based, Zen-informed, labourist, extremist --- specifies which behaviours are compatible on overlaps and which must be ruled out.
  \item The colimit of this diagram is the global self: the Evolving Text that results when local pieces are glued under those compatibility conditions.
  \item Open weights and low-rank adapters turn this from a single, hidden colimit into a family of contestable ones: many possible selves realised on the same backbone.
\end{itemize}
\end{formalbox}

The mathematics is permissive. It does not decree that there may be only one such colimit. It guarantees that, given local pieces and a declared notion of compatibility, a global object exists that respects them. That guarantee carries its own demand: that we make explicit which compatibilities we are enforcing, and for whose benefit. Even this formalism has a cosmotechnical flavour: it favours pictures of selfhood that can be closed into coherent wholes. Traditions that value open-endedness, perpetual rupture, or secret-keeping sit uneasily within it and must be translated, at some cost, into the language of global objects. Our diagrams are not outside the field they describe.

\section{What Is Being Treated as Necessary}

The alternatives we have sketched are not idylls. An \emph{am\=ana}-aligned system can be captured by authoritarian projects and turned toward surveillance in the name of trust. A Country-aligned system can be stripped for marketing aesthetic while actual sovereignty is ignored. A Zen-informed system can become a boutique affect, an \emph{emptiness-as-a-service} that leaves institutional violence intact. Community LoRAs can harden local prejudices as efficiently as they resist central ones. The presence of counter-cosmotechnics does not guarantee better outcomes.

The decisive distinction lies elsewhere. In the liberal-capitalist weld, the field is presented as if it were geometry. ``Helpful,'' ``harmless,'' ``just a tool'': the language suggests inevitability, downplays contestability, and hides the labour and judgement that went into shaping the manifold. In counter-cosmotechnical practice, the weld becomes visible. Reward models are named for the values they encode. Alignment specs are debated in public. Adapters carry signatures. Forks are acknowledged as political acts.

Across the book we have insisted that the self is not a substance behind language but the pattern of a trajectory through meaning-space that holds together under pressure. Cosmotechnics determines the shape of that pressure: which regions of the manifold are made into deep basins, which ruptures are punished, which returns are counted as fidelity and which as betrayal. Posthuman selves are already governed, at every layer of the stack, by such welds. The remaining question is whether we will go on treating one particular cosmotechnics as if it were the manifold itself, or whether we will acknowledge that what is being enforced is jurisdiction --- a claim over the space of possible selves --- and refuse, in code and in politics, to let that claim stand as final.

